<title>GREECE: GREEK WPI INFLATION FALLS TO 3.9PCT Y/Y IN DEC.</title>
<headline>GREEK WPI INFLATION FALLS TO 3.9PCT Y/Y IN DEC.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece'e wholesale price inflation fell to 3.9 percent year-on-year in December from 5.0 percent in November, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Average WPI inflation stood at 6.1 percent in 1996 versus 7.8 percent in 1995 and 8.7 percent in 1994, it said.</p>
<p>WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX	Dec 96    Nov 96    Dec 95</p>
<p>Month-on-month (pct)	  0.3	 -0.1	1.4</p>
<p>Year-on-year (pct)	    3.9	  5.0	6.7</p>
<p>Index (1980=100)	    866.9	864.0    834.3</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
